**Pattern (the wave's headline, §9 rule fired):** Amendment A13 — landed last cycle precisely to cure receipt incompleteness — met its first full wave, and **zero of five items cleared jev-prewave**. Every builder REPORTED its mechanical checks clean (harness assertions all PASS on all five final builds; A6 legs reported at 0 HITs on both legs for three items — T204 · T205 · T210 — with carried-with-disposition HITs on T199's fit leg and T208's census leg) — and three of those clean summaries were themselves found overstated by the re-fire returns (T204's fit row · T205's census rows · T205's CP01 PASS-at-0 ms against its failing 570 ms endpoint; §5 carries the itemized corrections) and every HOLD was ASSERTED-CHECKS on receipt grounds (the returns' own checking basis varies and is qualified in §9b.4 — T204/T210 are paperwork reviews; T205's re-fire independently evaluated its CP01 predicate and found the build failing the written strict bound, a stronger finding than a missing receipt): T199 (two index-line gaps in the fed paperwork, per its return's findings 1–2 and Limits: A-8's claimed probe inside the plate-owned window [0,800) has no filed dump in that window — the earliest filed dump is at 800 ms · B-17's swap receipt prints scale without the observed color the line claimed) · T204 (endpoint receipts + swap moved-instant receipts for five checkpoints + a fit row filed as a product instead of a measured bbox) · T205 (a strict-bound receipt failing at exactly 0.30 with no receipt at that instant · a fixed "8000ms" label in place of an evaluated instant · census rows overstating two phases' runtime effect) · T208 (timing-swap movement evidence for seven checkpoints via the inputs each assertion actually reads · a guard-#2 geometry receipt under content swap) · T210 (a hold-dependent swap probe · one stale index line printing a superseded value against its own receipt · CP9 without a whole-state equality receipt · palette swap without observed output values). The