**§9b — codex-condense firing 1 dispositions (REVISE, applied in full):**
1. *Candidate's causal claim corrected:* the §9 pattern's "same author writes the claim and checks it" is **consistent with the evidence, not established by it** — Wave 34 establishes that builder readiness checks let deficient receipts reach jev-prewave on all five items; it does not establish shared authorship as the cause or independence as the cure. The candidate stands NOT-YET-AMENDED with consumer HQ, its owning surfaces named: INSTRUCTION.md §5 leg 3b (the readiness step) + the mechanical guard layer (guards.md). **Acceptance test for HQ, from the filed failures:** any landed form must catch, on the filed Wave-34 records, (a) T199's A-8 — the exact probe and window a receipt claims must exist in the filed raw output (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md`, findings 1–2); (b) T199's B-17 — an observed swapped color must be printed by the swap receipt it is claimed under (same return); (c) T205's CP01 class — a binding predicate evaluated AT its endpoint (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 1: `stateAt(570 ms)` = exactly 0.30 against a strict < 0.30 bound). A grep-for-instant + CONFIG-diff check alone would miss (b) and (c) — the test says so on its face. The handoff's board state: HQ.json still carries this wave's Plan skeleton at firing time; the closed entry (§10 filings) is the handoff's confirmation.
2. *Mechanical guards, complete disposition:* command 4 (scores arithmetic) — **NOT DEMANDED this cycle** (no lens scores exist to consolidate; its non-firing is the two-HOLD rule's consequence, not an omission). Commands 2/6/7 — their REQUIREMENTS are sound; FOUR FINAL filed outputs were deficient (T208 + T210 under command 2 · T204 under command 6 · T205 under command 7 — the count is scoped to final outputs and is distinct from §5's three overstated clean-summary claims), which supports deferring a receipt-validation change to HQ rather than amending guard text here. **First-firing command-7 misses, recorded under the same deferral (firing 24):** the first prewave returns also caught census claims that had passed builder reconciliation and were cured before the final filings — T208's firing 1 (finding 3: overstated application sites for `countUpEasing` and `tileContrastGate`; the corrections stand recorded in its final config-census.md's application-site table + HIT list) · T205's firing 1 (the `content.blockLabel` coverage claim; the renderer branch added to cure it stands recorded in its final config-census.md's cure history). The recurring validation defect — census claims passing reconciliation at both firings — is owned by the same HQ deferral as the final-output deficiencies: command 2 (swap) — T208's re-fire found no regenerated-geometry result under content swap (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) AND T210's re-fire names command-2 output defects of its own: a stale swap instant in its index and palette swap without observed output values (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 6 (fit leg) — T204's swap-title fit row lacked a measured post-fit width (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`) · command 7 (census leg) — T205's census overstated two phases' runtime application (`hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md`, finding 3). Merely producing an output does not prove the guard was satisfied — §9's earlier per-command line stands corrected to this form. **Command 8 (census-anchor probes)** — its requirement is a raw probe at a named census instant WHERE THE CENSUS ASSERTS AN EMPTY OR ZERO STATE at that instant (the command's actual trigger, restored here at firing 10). T199's A-8 line claimed a probe inside the plate-owned interval [0,800) (its plan-amendment-cycle036.md), and the completion return's finding 1 distinguishes the filed CP8 dump at 7000 ms from the missing dump inside [0,800); the filed output carries no dump inside the interval (earliest filed dump at 800 ms). Whether the governing named census instant for that line is a specific instant inside the interval is NOT established on the filed record — **the command-8 assignment is left UNRESOLVED under HQ's deferral** rather than asserted. Independently of the assignment, the A13 receipt defect stands (an index line claiming evidence the filing does not contain). The command's text needs no change; VALIDATION of its filed outputs is part of the HQ deferral in §9b.1.
3. *Motion evidence + the observe-exit RETURN, re-disposed:* the T204 builder's receipt (32 frames inspected in sequence at 4 fps + two source stills) is **not** the continuous playback the gate requested, and T205's record likewise carries decoded-frame probes, not playback — the §1.2 continuous-playback debt names BOTH items (T204 · T205), and §2b's T205 line is corrected at firing 11 to match (its playback charge set aside with the gap carried, its ballot-timing charge applied). **Extended at firing 21 — T208 + T210: PLAYBACK UNVERIFIED.** Both items' Phase A records document firsthand inspection of extracted frames, and both observe-exit returns awarded full mechanics credit (1.0); neither record establishes that the item's original segment was watched in motion as §1.2 requires, and no filed playback receipt exists for either. They therefore join the same §1.2 debt in a second class — not a set-aside RETURN or charge (the gates ADVANCED both) but full mechanics credit awarded without the playback evidence the instruction requires. The deferred Jev question for the call file's next Condense now carries three members: (i) the §5 floor basis at exactly 0.5 · (ii) the FED-list receipt form · (iii) what evidence supports full mechanics credit — the T208/T210 advances priced against the same playback standard that RETURNed T204 at 0.5. The debt's full roster: T204 (RETURN set aside) · T205 (charge set aside) · T208 · T210 (playback unverified under full credit). The §2b disposition is therefore corrected: jev-observe-exit's T204 **RETURN-TO-OBSERVE is recorded as SET ASIDE with the gap carried** (the wave proceeded on census-proven mechanics; the playback evidence the call requires was never produced, and the gap is a standing Observe debt of this seat, named here rather than cured by relabeling). Two rule questions are priced for the call file's next Condense, NOT-YET-AMENDED with this reason: (i) the gate's §5 floor fires RETURN at any dimension **< 0.5**, and T204's mechanics scored exactly **0.5** — the RETURN therefore rests on the MECHANICS-UNSEEN taxonomy judgment, not the floor; whether a 0.5 mechanics score with complete frame evidence should RETURN is an unresolved rule question the return itself does not cite a basis for; (ii) the FED-list receipt-form change (§9's jev-observe-exit candidate) is deferred to the SAME Condense that prices (i) — both edits live in one call file, and piecemeal single-cycle edits to one call file are the divergence pattern this job has retired before. codex-observe's scope is the source-record audit (packet completeness · prior-attempt record · segment facts) — continuous-motion verification is the seat's §1.2 act, not that prompt's charge; the missed playback evidence is disposed as the seat's Observe defect above, not a codex-observe miss. Its NO-DEFECT line stands on that basis.
4. *Evidence binding (exact return paths):* T199 cross-cycle delta — prior re-fire `hidden_files/study/recreations/T199-shout-scaling-in-real-scene/codex/jev-prewave-refire.md` (0.75/1.00/0.40/0.75) → completion re-fire `…/codex/jev-prewave-completion2.md` (0.90/1.00/0.70/0.90). T204 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T204-dot-grid-identity-withheld-title/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T205 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T205-vote-to-grid-conversion-diagram/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T208 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T208-paired-dot-counts-house-stage/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. T210 — `hidden_files/study/recreations/T210-threshold-grid-map/codex/jev-prewave.md` → `…/jev-prewave-refire.md`. "Judges verified as real" in §9's pattern paragraph is qualified per §9b's head correction: each HOLD's grounds were checked on the basis its return states (paperwork review for T204/T210; independent predicate evaluation for T205's finding 1; harness re-run for T205's cure confirmations).
5. *Cost accounting corrected:* 25 firings before Condense (8 + 8 + 9), 26 including firing 1 of this close — §9 disposition 6 stands as corrected in place. A13's first full wave produced zero clearances; its effect on re-fire frequency remains **unestablished** (one wave, no clearance cohort to compare). The observed result, in place of any prediction language: four first attempts each used a re-fire, T199 used its carried completion re-fire, and none cleared (9 prewave firings, 0 waves spent).

