../../INSTRUCTION.md:23:- **Codex call point (Observe):** `guards/codex-observe.md` fires per item at §1 step 1 (source-record audit) on every cycle. Its receipts persist in RUN.md's Observe section; a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:24:- **Observe-exit call:** `guards/jev-observe-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the gate-out block per item before §2 opens for that item. The phase advances on the verdict's recorded disposition (applied, or set aside with reason; applied gaps are carried into §2 as named charges). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:30:4. **Verification plan:** swap test design (which config values change — at minimum the words; plus one timing and one palette value), purity checks (§6.1 greps + asset inventory), comparison sync method, and the Codex wave composition (four lenses, §5).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:33:- **Plan-exit call:** `guards/jev-plan-exit.md` fires at this gate on every cycle and judges the Plan product per item (parameter table · checklists · failure points · plateau priced in Plan per Amendment A2 — prior/family average + the stuck-lens hypothesis stated before Execute, not discovered at close) before §3 opens. `guards/codex-plan-review.md` fires alongside it for every item. Both verdicts are advisory: the phase advances on their recorded dispositions (applied, or set aside with reason). An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:49:3b. **Pre-wave Jev gate:** `guards/jev-prewave.md` judges the build record after legs 1–3 and before the wave (leg 4): FIRE-WAVE spends the wave; HOLD returns the build to Execute with its classification and the wave moves to its next item. **Receipt readiness check (Amendment A12, 2026-11-18 — performed by the builder BEFORE the payload is assembled):** every A11 checkpoint in the build-record carries its executable receipt — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A checkpoint with a claim but no receipt returns the record to the builder before the call is spent. **Receipt-index reconciliation (Amendment A13, 2026-11-18):** the build-record carries a RECEIPT INDEX enumerating (a) every guards.md command applicable to the item and (b) every A11 assertion for the item; before the payload is assembled the builder reconciles the index against the applicable guard commands, the item's planned A11 assertions, and — for a completion or re-attempt — the assertion sets established in the filed prior harnesses and their amendments, and, for census receipts, against the build's expected CONFIG keys (nested/array keys included). Every index line carries its executable receipt or an explicit NOT-DEMANDED line whose disposition cites the governing plan or guard; a missing expected line, an unsupported exclusion, or a line with neither returns the record to the builder. A receipt is valid only if it carries the evidence its assertion requires: for each CONFIG-derived input, the CONFIG expression and its evaluated value; for each check, the raw observed result. A populated receipt lacking that evidence returns the record to the builder on the same form. This check is a readiness check for the mandatory call, not a gate on it: the call still fires at its step on every cycle, and a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE under the standing firing ruling. The deliverable-class judgment for this job IS the five-lens scoring wave (leg 4, defined in `guards/codex-scoring-wave.md`) — no separate jev-verify file exists, by design: the wave's per-lens verdicts + leg 5's mechanical consolidation are the deliverable gate, and a second Jev over the same deliverable would duplicate them.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:51:5. **Consolidation verdict (mechanical):** average of the five lens scores ≥85 AND minimum lens ≥70 → PASS. Else FAIL. The arithmetic is shown in scores.md; no rounding up across the bar.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:52:Gate out: scores.md complete (four lens scores + returns pointers + verdict + arithmetic); tier hand-off filed to style-library (its board) with the verdict; TECHNIQUES/INDEX tier moves are style-library's act.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:57:3. **Scoring integrity:** four lenses, four separate runs, returns filed verbatim before the verdict is computed; a missing lens = no verdict (the wave is incomplete, printed as such). Scores from a prior attempt never carry into a new attempt's average.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:84:3. **THE FIFTH LENS — READABILITY (permanent, §5.4):** the founding evidence is priced: four lenses scored a recreation whose words fight their own background, and none owned legibility. The owner's expectation now has a judge (the golden rule). Attempt 2 onward is scored by five lenses; the bar form is unchanged (average ≥85, no lens <70) with the fifth lens inside both terms. Attempts scored under the four-lens wave keep their filed averages — cross-wave comparisons print the lens count (a 4-lens 78.5 and a 5-lens score are different instruments; deltas across the boundary are labeled as such).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:87:## §9 — Condense
../../INSTRUCTION.md:89:- **Condense Codex call point:** `guards/codex-condense.md` fires at Condense close — it attacks the cycle's drafted amendments for faithfulness (does the amended text encode the lesson) and four-layer coverage (steps · mechanical guards · Jev definitions · Codex prompts; each untouched layer carries a NO-DEFECT proof or a named not-yet-amended reason). A REVISE returns the named amendment for re-encoding before the cycle record closes. Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle; a cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE. (Built 2026-11-14.)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:92:- Completion reported on this job's HQ.json + lane heartbeat: technique, attempt #, five lens scores + average, verdict, artifact path.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:96:Before this job's Condense closes, every cycle, evaluate the judgment layer AS HOSTED IN THIS JOB'S OWN HOME (the `guards/` directory at the home root): (a) every judge this job's deliverables demand is present as its own file there — Jev calls (instruction + call command), deterministic guards, Codex review instructions for the review types this job repeats; (b) each is current against this cycle's experience (a verdict reversed, a defect that passed, a review that missed — each either amended its file in this Condense or is named in the cycle record as not-yet-amended with its reason); (c) any judge the deliverable demanded this cycle that does not exist yet is CREATED in this step or carried as a named build charge with pilot sequencing — never noted-and-dropped. The verdict prints in the cycle record: **JUDGMENT LAYER: COMPLETE** (all demanded judges hosted + current) or **INCOMPLETE** (missing/stale judges named). INCOMPLETE is a lawful print; a silent Condense is not. JOB-05's census reads this field fleet-wide.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:97:Founding print (2026-11-14): JUDGMENT LAYER: **INCOMPLETE** — mechanical guards hosted + demonstrated (5/5); Codex scoring wave defined in-job and demonstrated in four-lens form (five-lens form demonstrates at its first wave); jev-prewave designed, **UNBUILT** — build charge carried in this job's Condense until armed.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:99:**Ruling addendum (2026-11-14 ~20:55 EST — owner's judgment-call ruling):** arming = firing. This job's Jev/Codex steps are non-skippable and fire unconditionally in its next live cycle, raw responses filed in the run record; verdicts are advisory — applied, or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense + the call-file amendment it teaches. The founding print above reads superseded where it phrases any call as gated, conditional, or UNBUILT-blocked; presence from the next cycle prices whether the prescribed firings HAPPENED (a cycle closing without one is INCOMPLETE).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:102:The measured-fit leg and the config-census leg — candidacy text since Waves 5–6 — are built as standing guards: `guards/guard-measured-fit.md` and `guards/guard-config-census.md` (v3.1 codified, including application-site resolution for nested/array keys and the CSS-variable setter check). **Pre-wave step (non-skippable):** for every item in a wave, after the build and BEFORE the five-lens scoring wave fires, both legs run on the item's final recreation.html and their outputs file in the item's artifact directory (`fit-table.md`, `config-census.md`); the wave RUN cites each leg's path + hit count per item. A wave record lacking either leg's output for any item prints **INCOMPLETE**. Leg verdicts are advisory (owner's 2026-11-14 ruling): hits are cured pre-scoring where the builder can, or carried into the wave printed with their disposition; misses (a leg's false hit or missed defect) are recorded in Condense with the guard-file amendment they teach. Scope: the legs own the fit and config classes only — timing anchors, density judgment, and content failures are NOT theirs and are never presented as cured by them.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:105:**Schedule basis is a required Plan field.** The §9 pattern rule fired this cycle: two techniques' timing lenses independently priced the same defect class — a recreation whose schedule is silently re-based from the segment's measured timeline (T64 lens-timing −16: calendar entrances at 0.4/1.4 s vs measured ~4/5 s · T66 lens-timing-interim1 −18: opening state mismatching the measured window). Standing requirement, binding on every Plan from Wave 12 onward: each item's window-scope line in the wave RUN.md names its **schedule basis** — `segment-anchored` (the build's phases sit at their measured segment times), `t=0 allocation` (the technique's lifecycle is re-based to the build's own zero, with the re-basing named as an allocation), or `two-act` (a measured-window act plus a labeled allocation-model act) — and the item's build-record carries the same line. A Plan whose window-scope line lacks the schedule basis is incomplete in the same way a Plan lacking its swap values is (jev-plan-exit prices it). Landed by Cycle 013's Condense under the pattern rule; HQ may amend or retire it, and until then it is operative instruction, not candidacy.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:107:## Amendment A9 (2026-11-16, Cycle 023 Condense — the five Cycle-022 NOT-YET-AMENDED landings, plus this cycle's pattern promotion)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:108:Landed by Cycle 023's first Replan item, the named consumer of Cycle 022 §9's five outstanding amendments. Each clause is operative instruction, binding from Wave 21 onward.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:114:6. **Parameterization depth (A9.6 — pattern promotion, §9 rule: the reusability finding recurred across T139 + T140 in Cycle 023, both lens-minimum at 78).** Every subject-shaping value is CONFIG data, not a code literal: vehicle/geometry branch data, background-layer geometry and growth/opacity coefficients (a background layer's coefficients are subject-shaping when a lens can price them against the subject — the T140 dust classification is resolved this way), and plate tile data. The config-census leg (A6) prices literals of these classes as HITs from Wave 21 onward; guard-config-census.md's classification text is amended in the same landing's guard sweep or carries the not-yet-amended note in the cycle record that first applies it.
../../INSTRUCTION.md:117:Landed by Cycle 026's Condense, discharging the carry recorded in Cycle 025 §9 item 1 and Cycle 026 §0b item 1. Each clause restates at instruction level a form already operative in the guards or gate contracts; each is binding from Wave 23 onward (Wave 23 complied with all three, filed in its run record).
../../INSTRUCTION.md:122:## Amendment A11 (2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense — census-checkpoint assertions; adopting the practice job's census-checkpoint note, practice Cycle 019 Condense, carried as a candidate by Cycle 027 §9.1 and adopted here on three independent demonstrations)
../../INSTRUCTION.md:126:1. **Receipt form (operative step: §5 leg 3b's readiness check, referenced from §3 step 4).** Every A11 assertion in a build-record files its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT beside the claim — the harness command or run, the CONFIG expression evaluated, and the raw result from the build under review; for a CONFIG timing swap the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant. A9.4 already required raw output; this clause names the receipt's three parts and wires the check into the prewave step itself. A build-record whose assertions carry claims without receipts is incomplete at the builder's own gate: jev-prewave is not spent on it (the call's firing obligation is unchanged — the readiness check precedes payload assembly, and an unfired call still prints the cycle INCOMPLETE).
../../guards/codex-condense.md:6:1. **Consumer:** recreation's §9 Condense for the closing cycle + the decision priced: whether the cycle's lessons were faithfully encoded into the instruction layer (steps · mechanical guards · Jev definitions · Codex prompts), or whether an amendment claims a lesson its text does not carry.
../../guards/codex-condense.md:11:Fires at §9 Condense close, after the cycle's amendments are drafted and before the cycle record closes. The run attacks:
../../guards/codex-condense.md:12:- **Faithfulness of each amendment:** for every lesson promoted this cycle (dated, technique cited — §9 form), does the amended instruction/guard text actually encode the lesson such that a cold builder following only the text would behave differently? An amendment that names a cure in prose while leaving the operative step unchanged is classified AMENDMENT-THEATRE. Founding calibration shape: Amendment A5 — Owner Cures 1+2 landed as construction requirements AND a fifth lens in §5.4 AND flow-field guidance; a lesser encoding (a mention in a lessons list) would have failed this attack.
../../guards/codex-condense.md:13:- **Four-layer coverage:** did this cycle's experience touch each layer — (1) instruction steps, (2) mechanical guard code/commands (guards.md), (3) Jev definitions (jev-prewave · jev-observe-exit · jev-plan-exit), (4) Codex prompts (codex-scoring-wave · codex-observe · codex-plan-review · this file) — and for each untouched layer, is the no-change a NO-DEFECT proof naming the evidence checked, or an escape? A reversed verdict, a defect that passed a gate, or a lens finding that recurred across two techniques (§9 pattern rule) MUST land on its owning layer or be named not-yet-amended with reason (the presence-evaluation rule).
../../guards/codex-condense.md:19:- ONE stream: this instruction + the cycle's RUN.md + the amendment diffs drafted this Condense (before/after text) + the §9 candidate-lesson list — never pipe + stdin together (fleet rule).
../../guards/codex-condense.md:23:- **DEFINED** (2026-11-14). **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** No run has fired under this definition; Cycles 001–002 Condensed without it (their amendments A1–A5 stand as filed; this review prices future Condenses, it does not retro-judge them). First demonstration: the next recreation wave's Condense.
../../guards/guard-config-census.md:11:`config-census.md` in the item's artifact directory: literal count by class with the per-constant classification, the key→site resolution table, the CSS-variable check, and a HIT list (empty = PASS for this leg). The wave's RUN cites the path + hit count per item. The leg's verdict is ADVISORY (owner's 2026-11-14 ruling): hits are cured before scoring where the builder can, or carried into the wave printed with their disposition. The FIRING is not advisory: a wave whose record lacks the census for any item prints INCOMPLETE.
../../guards/codex-observe.md:24:- **DEFINED** (2026-11-14). **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** No run has fired under this definition; T15 attempt 1 (2026-11-13) predates it and ran no Observe-phase Codex audit. First demonstration: the next recreation wave's first item with a prior family record (expected: a particle-family or typography-family item citing T15).
../../guards/jev-plan-exit.md:7:- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §2, at the gate out of Plan, before §3 Execute opens for an item. The verdict is advisory per item — applied, or set aside with the miss recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../guards/jev-plan-exit.md:11:(1) PARAMETER TABLE COMPLETE — every variable from the Observe gate-out (§1.3 list, as passed by jev-observe-exit) is a named config key with the specimen's value as default (§2.1). A variable with no key, or animation logic the Plan already describes with literals, is a Plan failure named here — not an Execute surprise.
../../guards/jev-plan-exit.md:37:- Defined prompt + context assembly per §3, executed through the fleet's sealed decision-model route named in guards.md when bound. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.**
../../guards/jev-plan-exit.md:44:Amendments name forcing evidence + before/after. A text change takes effect on the call's next firing; the call keeps firing every cycle, and Condense prices the change against the returns that follow it. Standing watch: whether the §2.4 "four lenses" wording anywhere still survives against the five-lens form — any Plan citing four lenses is a FAILURE-POINTS-GENERIC signal, not a typo.
../../guards/jev-plan-exit.md:48:**Forcing evidence (three instances, one class):** T153 Wave 21 (timing 45 — §2b allocation contradicted the §1c census checkpoints it claimed to rest on) · T160 Wave 22 (timing 68 — prescribed onsets 2500/3500 ms already 8.33%/45.45% grown at the 449 s/452 s census instants) · T162 Wave 22 (timing 64 — even-stepped allocation completing at 11300 ms against census anchors at ~2000/~7000 ms). For T160 and T162 the build implemented the prescribed schedule exactly (verified from this cycle's filed returns, bound in Cycle 025 RUN §9b item 2); for T153 the same compliance is attributed to the seat's Wave-21 cycle record (Cycle 024 RUN §5) and is unverified in the Wave-22 stream. In all three the defect was the Plan's, discovered by the timing lens at the cost of the item's verdict.
../../guards/guard-measured-fit.md:13:`fit-table.md` in the item's artifact directory: the full row set (each row carrying its instrument/provenance per check 1; stand-in rows labeled PROXY with the font named) + a HIT list (empty = PASS for this leg). The wave's RUN cites the table's path + hit count per item. The leg's verdict is ADVISORY (owner's 2026-11-14 ruling): hits are priced into the build before scoring where the builder can cure them; hits carried into the scoring wave are printed in the RUN with their disposition. What is NOT advisory is the firing: a wave whose record lacks the fit table for any item prints INCOMPLETE.
../../guards/BUILD-LOG.md:24:- §9 Condense: codex-condense call point (four-layer iteration + presence evaluation already stood in the closing section; confirmed standing, not re-added).
../../guards/BUILD-LOG.md:27:- No `jev-verify-*.md` — per the tasking and the spec's extension rule: this job's deliverable Jevs are the per-technique lens waves (codex-scoring-wave.md, five lenses incl. READABILITY); duplicating them as a Jev would create a second, divergent deliverable standard.
../../guards/BUILD-LOG.md:34:- Standing inconsistency the new gates will catch, not fixed by this pass (insertions-only rule): INSTRUCTION §2.4 still says "four lenses" in the verification-plan line while §5 carries the five-lens form — jev-plan-exit §7 names a four-lens Plan citation as a defect signal; the §2.4 wording correction is a Condense amendment for the job itself, not this build pass.
../../guards/jev-prewave.md:7:- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §4, between the builder's own checks (§5.2) and the wave (§5.3). The verdict is advisory: applied, a HOLD returns the build to the builder with named defects and the wave does not fire on that item; set aside, the miss is recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../guards/jev-prewave.md:10:Judge whether this build record shows a recreation ready to be scored, or one whose defects are already visible in its own paperwork. Price: (1) PARAMETERIZATION — is the piece genuinely CONFIG-driven (fields named, ranges sane), or hard-coded with a config costume? (2) PURITY PRE-CHECK — does the construction route describe generation from parameters, with no tracing/embedding step hiding in the prose? (3) OWN-CHECKS COMPLETENESS — are the mechanical guards' results recorded (purity grep, swap test, syntax), or asserted? **Census-checkpoint mapping (Amendment A11, landed 2026-11-17, Cycle 028 Condense): every Observe census checkpoint for the item must map to an executable own-check assertion whose evaluation instant is CONFIG-derived; the build-record identifies checkpoint · assertion · CONFIG expression · evaluated result. ASSERTED-CHECKS is returned if any checkpoint lacks this mapping, any evaluation instant uses hardcoded defaults, or execution evidence is absent; a CONFIG timing swap must be shown to move the corresponding assertion's evaluation instant. Receipt form (Amendment A12, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 035 Condense): the execution evidence for each assertion is its EXECUTABLE RECEIPT — harness command or run · CONFIG expression evaluated · raw result from the build under review (for a timing swap, the receipt shows the changed evaluation instant); a claim without its receipt is execution evidence absent. **Receipt-index ground (Amendment A13, landed 2026-11-18, Cycle 036 Condense): a build-record whose RECEIPT INDEX (INSTRUCTION A13.1) is missing an expected entry (an applicable guards.md command, a planned A11 assertion, an assertion inherited whole from a prior attempt's filed harness, or a census row for an expected CONFIG key), carries an exclusion whose disposition cites no governing plan or guard, or carries a populated receipt lacking the evidence its assertion requires (CONFIG expression + evaluated value for CONFIG-derived inputs; raw observed result for checks) is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground by name.** The same leg prices the A6 fit evidence: a fit-table row lacking measurement provenance, or carrying model-derived bounds, per guard-measured-fit.md checks 1–2 is an ASSERTED-CHECKS ground.** (4) TECHNIQUE FIDELITY PLAN — does the record state which packet mechanics the build implements and which it deliberately defers (a deferral named is lawful; a mechanic silently absent is not)? Score 0–1 per dimension, classify defects. You judge paperwork only: a build can pass you and still fail its wave — your job is that no wave is spent on a build its own record already condemns.
../../guards/codex-scoring-wave.md:6:Five independent lens runs score ONE recreation attempt against the BAR: **average of the five lens scores ≥ 85 AND no lens < 70** (the recreation law; a pass at this bar is the only route to RECREATED).
../../guards/codex-scoring-wave.md:12:- **Identical-hash binding (ADOPTED 2026-11-14, Cycle 009):** all five returns of an attempt must bind to the identical final recreation.html SHA-256. When a lens catches an interim-build defect, the build is cured, self-verify re-runs, and the wave re-fires on the final build; the interim return is preserved verbatim (e.g. `codex/lens-motion-interim1.md`) and never enters the final average. Founding instance: Wave 6, T38 (interim motion 35 → cured → five lenses re-fired on the final build).
../../guards/codex-scoring-wave.md:34:**Divergence notice (2026-11-17, practice Cycle-022 Condense, consumed at its Codex Condense REGRADE finding 2):** practice's wave file (`study-jobs/practice/guards/codex-rescore-wave.md`) diverged further by **A-C022-2 (scratch-cwd trust flag, CANDIDATE, practice-only firing-form)**. The five lenses and the bar agree across both files. Adoption here is recreation's own Condense decision.
../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md:7:- Call point: recreation INSTRUCTION §1, at the gate out of Observe, before §2 Plan opens for any item in the wave. The verdict is advisory per item: applied, a RETURN-TO-OBSERVE item is held out of the wave's Plan (the wave proceeds with its advancing items; a held item never holds the wave hostage — same rule as jev-prewave §5); set aside, the miss is recorded in Condense. An unfired call makes the cycle INCOMPLETE.
../../guards/jev-observe-exit.md:37:- Defined prompt + context assembly per §3, executed through the fleet's sealed decision-model route named in guards.md when bound. Binding the exact runner command here is the first firing's own first step. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.**
../../guards/codex-plan-review.md:24:- **DEFINED** (2026-11-14). **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** No run has fired under this definition. First demonstration: the next wave item in the particle or typography family (T15's machinery siblings head the queue's priced reasons — T16 at queue #11 shares the pool; T03 at #2 heads the unattempted queue).
../../guards/guards.md:18:6. **Measured-fit leg** — `guard-measured-fit.md` in this directory. Per item, pre-wave: every subject text element carries a MEASURED fit row (post-fit ink bounds vs container at the 360 px stage, legibility floor ~11 px); a formula-claimed fit or a missing row is a HIT. Owns the "fit asserted, not measured" readability class (Waves 2–5, 10). **Built 2026-11-15 (HQ owed-checks charge); fires unconditionally at the pre-wave step from the next cycle; a wave record lacking a fit table for any item prints INCOMPLETE.** Verdict advisory; firing is not.
../../guards/guards.md:19:7. **Config-census leg (v3.1 codified)** — `guard-config-census.md` in this directory. Per item, pre-wave: all-literal scan with per-constant subject-shaping/structural classification + CONFIG key→application-site resolution (nested/array keys included) + CSS-variable setter check; unapplied keys and unset-variable references are HITs. Owns the config-incompleteness reusability class. **Built 2026-11-15 (HQ owed-checks charge); fires unconditionally at the pre-wave step from the next cycle; a wave record lacking a census for any item prints INCOMPLETE.** Verdict advisory; firing is not.
../../guards/guards.md:22:- `jev-prewave.md` — judges a build record's readiness to spend a scoring wave. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (Designed 2026-11-14; attempt 1 predates it and ran under the §5 panel, which runs alongside.)
../../guards/guards.md:23:- `jev-observe-exit.md` — the Observe→Plan gate for a recreation wave (queue state priced · prior/family scores read · mechanics seen · variables extracted · flow-field model + Owner Cures 1–2 carried in working memory · consumer named). Call point: INSTRUCTION §1 gate out. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (Phase-guard augmentation, 2026-11-14.)
../../guards/guards.md:24:- `jev-plan-exit.md` — the Plan→Execute gate (parameter table · Execute + Verify checklists as instruments · failure points priced · plateau floor rule priced in Plan). Call point: INSTRUCTION §2 gate out. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (2026-11-14.)
../../guards/guards.md:28:- `codex-scoring-wave.md` — the five-lens scoring wave (motion fidelity · timing/tempo · construction purity · reusability · readability). Demonstrated: 2026-11-13, T15 attempt 1 (four lenses then; readability added 2026-11-14 under the owner's order — the five-lens form demonstrates at the next wave).
../../guards/guards.md:29:- `codex-observe.md` — Observe-phase source-record audit (packet-section completeness · prior-attempt record audit · segment facts). Call point: INSTRUCTION §1 step 1, per item. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (2026-11-14.)
../../guards/guards.md:30:- `codex-plan-review.md` — Plan attack priced against this job's recorded failure modes (convergent freeze · owner's two catches · parameterization reality · bar arithmetic · §8 size discipline). Call point: INSTRUCTION §2 gate out, alongside jev-plan-exit. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (2026-11-14.)
../../guards/guards.md:31:- `codex-condense.md` — Condense review: amendment faithfulness + four-layer coverage attack. Call point: INSTRUCTION §9, at Condense close. Consumer: the job's next cycle. **Firing: this call fires at its step on every cycle. A cycle in which it did not fire prints INCOMPLETE.** (2026-11-14.)
../../guards/guards.md:38:JUDGMENT LAYER: **INCOMPLETE** — mechanical guards hosted + demonstrated (5/5); Codex wave defined in-job and demonstrated (four-lens form; five-lens form pending its first wave); jev-prewave designed, DEFINED — it fires at its step on every cycle.
../../guards/guards.md:41:JUDGMENT LAYER: **INCOMPLETE** — phase-transition layer now hosted: jev-observe-exit + jev-plan-exit (both DEFINED) · codex-observe + codex-plan-review + codex-condense (all DEFINED) · jev-prewave DEFINED · five-lens scoring wave still pending its first demonstration. Every call in this layer fires at its step on every cycle; a cycle in which one did not fire prints INCOMPLETE. Build record: `BUILD-LOG.md` in this directory.
../../guards/guards.md:44:ARMING = FIRING abolishes the arming states printed in this index: this job's calls are DEFINED and fire unconditionally in its next live cycle (raw responses filed in the run record); verdicts are advisory (applied, or set aside with the miss + the call-file amendment recorded in Condense). The founding Presence print stands as the 2026-11-14 founding record; from the next cycle, the presence evaluation prices FIRING (fired / not fired — not fired = INCOMPLETE), not arming.
